# Writing posts (rishi23root.in)

Follow `web/BLOG_WRITING_GUIDE.md`. Short version:

- Write as Rishabh (first person, plain, specific). No hype or filler.
- Section order for Writing posts (as `##` headings, after the `title` H1): TL;DR → What problem I had → What I tried → What worked → What failed → Architecture → Code → Results → What I recommend. A short qualifier after a colon is fine; drop a section that has nothing real rather than pad it. Skeleton: `content/posts/draft-template.mdx`.
- The TL;DR answers the title in 1-2 sentences.
- `##`/`###` headings only (the H1 comes from `title`). Code fences need a language. Images need alt text.
- Frontmatter: `title` ≤ 90 chars, one-sentence `summary` ≤ 220, kebab-case `slug` equal to the file name, `date` YYYY-MM-DD. Optional: `tags`, `updated`, `primaryKeyword`, `secondaryKeywords`, `seoTitle`, `cover`, `image`, `faq` (2-4 stand-alone Q&A).
- `<Callout tone="answer|note|warning">` is available in MDX without an import. Use it sparingly.
- `<ExcalidrawBoard src="/diagrams/<name>.json" />` embeds a read-only diagram rendered to SVG (no import). Scenes live in `web/public/diagrams/`; see the "Excalidraw boards" section in `AGENTS.md`.
- Never publish secrets, client or employer data, other people's personal data, unbacked claims, uncredited copy, or unreviewed AI text.
- New posts start from `content/posts/draft-template.mdx` with `draft: true`. Flip it to `false` only after the checklist in the guide passes and `npm run build:web` is green.
